    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Maths feels like a puzzle I’m still figuring out—like solving a board game’s rules step by step. My parents struggled with it too, so I approach it cautiously but enjoy the logic behind equations and patterns. It’s not intimidating; it’s more about curiosity than fear.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Sometimes, especially if I’m stuck on a problem or see abstract symbols, my mind races like a baking timer—too fast to think clearly. But I remind myself math is just language, and I’ve got the tools (and my agreeable nature) to break it down.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "No, but if I had tried, I’d imagine using an AI like a baking recipe—step-by-step guidance. It might feel overwhelming at first (like extraversion’s highs and lows), but the structured answers could help me avoid neuroticism spirals over complex problems.",
